WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
A pure tone is a vibration of air
back and forth at a certain frequency.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.700
And it sounds like this.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.220
[tone]

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.760
If you want to raise the pitch of that tone,
you can speed up those vibrations.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.660
[higher, shorter tone]

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:15.120
But because you've sped the vibrations up,
that tone doesn't last as long.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.300
Slow it down...

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.000
[lower, longer tone]

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.520
...and that tone will go on for longer.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.780
Pitch correction, or auto-tune, is clever.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.180
When it changes a note that someone's
not quite sung correctly,

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.220
it changes the speed of the vibrations,

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.700
but it also adds or removes some vibrations
so the duration stays the same.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.520
Except that's not quite the full answer.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.860
Because musical notes don't sound like this:

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.960
[tone]

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.720
They sound like this.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.620
- ♫ Hello ♫
- ♫ Hello! ♫

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.200
- ♫ Hello... ♫
- ♫ Hello~ ♫

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.460
Ladies, gentlemen,
and all in between,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.040
the Gregory Brothers.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.280
♫

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.720
 

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.980
 

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.640
 

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.000
 

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.140
 

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.920
 

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.220
 

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.400
 

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.940
 

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:33.340
 

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.720
 

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.580
 

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.940
 

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:51.380
 

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.260
 

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.640
 

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.860
 

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.500
 

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.520
♫ Oh yeah, some talent's still require~d ♫

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.520
[effects and auto-tune fade out]

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.980
[note continues]

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.880
[gasps]

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.300
- I know we're wandering off,
but I thought that sounded pretty good.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.900
- That certainly worked for me.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.260
[laughter]

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.260
- That's good.
- It's a powerful note.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.860
- That hurt! That actually hurt.

